(PRC-36 — the list-variable form: argv is built at runtime from the list's
 current length and contents, so a list grown by `append` after it was
 declared is passed in full.
 Also covers: PRC-37 (argv is sized from that single length read; an empty
 list gives argc 1 and does not overrun — the empty case was run
 separately and printed `argc=1` through the argv-dumping helper of
 PRC-34).
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-36.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   count=3 first=alpha last=gamma
)
a list called 'the command arguments' is ["-c"].
append "echo count=$# first=$1 last=$3" to 'the command arguments'.
append "shell-name" to 'the command arguments'.
append "alpha" to 'the command arguments'.
append "beta" to 'the command arguments'.
append "gamma" to 'the command arguments'.
Execute "/bin/sh" with arguments 'the command arguments'.
On error print "the exec failed".
